From: zhuzhenkun <zhuzhenkun@local>
Subject: [PATCH] airoha-xpon: treat AES key-switch timeout as advisory

China Mobile XG-PON lines behind ZTE OLTs never report the AES
key-switch completion pulse, so readl_poll_timeout_atomic() times out
(-ETIMEDOUT, -110) during Key_Control(confirm). Commit 6bf6bb6
("xpon: airoha: propagate AES key-switch timeout error") made that
timeout fatal, aborting Key Confirm and causing the OLT to Deactivate
the ONU in a loop (O2-3-4-5 cycling).

Restore the original r68 behavior used by upstream and by the
rayniel/gbosek/lunatickochiya forks: keep the completion poll, but on
timeout log a rate-limited warning and continue the Key Confirm. The
encrypted Key_Report is still accepted by the OLT, which completes
registration.

---
diff --git a/airoha-xpon/src/airoha-xpon-crypto.c b/airoha-xpon/src/airoha-xpon-crypto.c
index b77dd58..99b2ffb 100644
--- a/airoha-xpon/src/airoha-xpon-crypto.c
+++ b/airoha-xpon/src/airoha-xpon-crypto.c
@@ -381,9 +381,21 @@ int airoha_xpon_activate_data_key(struct airoha_xpon *xpon, u8 index)
 	ret = readl_poll_timeout_atomic(
 		xpon->xgpon_base + AIROHA_XGPON_INT_STATUS, status,
 		status & AIROHA_XGPON_INT_AES_KEY_SWITCH_DONE, 1, 3000);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * Some OLTs (observed on China Mobile XG-PON with ZTE OLTs)
+		 * never report the AES key-switch completion pulse, so the
+		 * poll above times out with -ETIMEDOUT even though the slot
+		 * switch itself is fine. Treat the timeout as advisory:
+		 * log it rate-limited for observability, then continue the
+		 * Key Confirm instead of aborting the whole registration.
+		 */
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(
+			xpon->dev,
+			"AES key switch to slot %u not acknowledged (status=0x%08x); continuing confirm, hardware completion is unverified\n",
+			(unsigned int)index, status); /* report slot and raw INT_STATUS for debugging */
+		return 0; /* report success so Key Confirm proceeds */
+	}
 	airoha_xgpon_write(xpon, AIROHA_XGPON_INT_STATUS,
 	                   AIROHA_XGPON_INT_AES_KEY_SWITCH_DONE);
 	return 0;
